{"id":"ed21199fbef98411","group":"67","path":"67/67-df-degree-finite-generation.md","title":"Finite Joins of Low Complexity Degrees","display":"df-degree-finite-generation — Finite Joins of Low Complexity Degrees","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom","book_abbrev":"67","label":"67-df-degree-finite-generation","aliases":["67-df-degree-finite-generation"],"display":"df-degree-finite-generation — Finite Joins of Low Complexity Degrees","depends_on":["[[67-df-degree-complexity]]","[[67-df-degree-bounds]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf","source_edition":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition","source_chapter":"7","source_label":"definitions of E_T and F_T before Theorems 7.12 and 7.13","source_printed_pages":[106,107],"source_pdf_pages":[117,118],"verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"definition-and-signature-checked","eligible_as_verified_dependency":true},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"67"},{"key":"label","html":"67-df-degree-finite-generation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67-df-degree-finite-generation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-degree-finite-generation — Finite Joins of Low Complexity Degrees"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"73717706953334f5\" href=\"?note=73717706953334f5\" title=\"67-df-degree-complexity\">67-df-degree-complexity</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"511859971a231477\" href=\"?note=511859971a231477\" title=\"67-df-degree-bounds\">67-df-degree-bounds</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_chapter","html":"7"},{"key":"source_label","html":"definitions of E_T and F_T before Theorems 7.12 and 7.13"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>106</span><span>107</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>117</span><span>118</span></div>"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"definition-and-signature-checked"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"true"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D_T,\\mathsf S_T,\\mathsf P_T\">\\(D_T,\\mathsf S_T,\\mathsf P_T\\)</span> 采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"73717706953334f5\" href=\"?note=73717706953334f5\" title=\"67-df-degree-complexity\">67-df-degree-complexity</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sup}_T\">\\(\\mathrm{Sup}_T\\)</span> 采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"511859971a231477\" href=\"?note=511859971a231477\" title=\"67-df-degree-bounds\">67-df-degree-bounds</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Fin}(X)\">\\(\\operatorname{Fin}(X)\\)</span> 表示集合 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> 的全部有限子集，含空集。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf E_T,\\mathsf F_T\">\\(\\mathsf E_T,\\mathsf F_T\\)</span> 是下式构造的度集合。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Fin}(X)\\coloneqq\\{H\\subseteq X:|H|&lt;\\aleph_0\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{Fin}(X)\\coloneqq\\{H\\subseteq X:|H|&lt;\\aleph_0\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf E_T\\coloneqq\\{c\\in D_T:\\exists H\\in\\operatorname{Fin}(\\mathsf S_T)\\;\\mathrm{Sup}_T(H,c)\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathsf E_T\\coloneqq\\{c\\in D_T:\\exists H\\in\\operatorname{Fin}(\\mathsf S_T)\\;\\mathrm{Sup}_T(H,c)\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf F_T\\coloneqq\\{c\\in D_T:\\exists H\\in\\operatorname{Fin}(\\mathsf S_T\\cup\\mathsf P_T)\\;\\mathrm{Sup}_T(H,c)\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathsf F_T\\coloneqq\\{c\\in D_T:\\exists H\\in\\operatorname{Fin}(\\mathsf S_T\\cup\\mathsf P_T)\\;\\mathrm{Sup}_T(H,c)\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书印刷106页/PDF117页定义 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E_T\">\\(E_T\\)</span> 为有限组 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_1\">\\(\\Sigma_1\\)</span> 度的并，印刷106–107页/PDF117–118页定义 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F_T\">\\(F_T\\)</span> 为有限组 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_1\">\\(\\Sigma_1\\)</span> 和 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi_1\">\\(\\Pi_1\\)</span> 度的并。这里明确有限性及空组的底元约定，并用上确界关系给出集合构造。</p>\n<p>这里讨论的是解释度格的并，不是代表句的析取，也不是公理集并。原书定理12、13给出这两种生成方式的限制，见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d45c90153d8ba06e\" href=\"?note=d45c90153d8ba06e\" title=\"67-thm-degree-finite-generation-gap\">67-thm-degree-finite-generation-gap</a>。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-df-degree-complexity","status":"resolved","id":"73717706953334f5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 